            <ArticleTitle>Acute scrotal symptoms due to perforated appendix in children: case report and review of literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>181-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute appendicitis is rarely included in the differential diagnosis of acute scrotum. We report a case of an unusual presentation of acute appendicitis as acute left scrotal swelling. The relevant literature is reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
